#! A module import, a column choice, and a published view.
#!
#! `select {.a, .b}` chooses columns and `update` recomputes or renames them;
#! both are used here, and the difference between them is the difference
#! between this file and `schema.cagara`.
import "schema.cagara" as s

## Drop `password_hash` by selecting only the columns that are published, and
## give `name` its public label. Named a projection, not an update: the result
## row is exactly the field list.
public_users = s.users & select { .id, display_name = .name }

## The definition `cagara public.cagara` prints — the view this module exists
## to publish. A file runs one query, and `main` is how it says which.
main = public_users
